Notebook[{
Cell["Lesson 13 - Dimensions", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"d15e408e-fc73-4f54-a3b2-470d0e41bb8c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Physics step.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Derive the scaling dimension of every coupling, every field and of time \
from the requirement that ",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalGamma]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "_k = ",
 StyleBox["\[Integral]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "dt d",
 StyleBox["\:1d48",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "x ",
 StyleBox["\|01d4db",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " is dimensionless, with [x] = 1/k. The dimensions are written in a basis \
you choose: the RG scale k and N + 1 ",
 StyleBox["reference couplings",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (N = number of scalars), whose running defines the anomalous dimensions, \
",
 StyleBox["\[PartialD]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "s ref = ",
 StyleBox["\[Minus]\[Eta]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " ref. This module needs only the ansatz, so it can run right after lesson \
02, before any loop."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9961d01d-e3a6-4659-b507-691a7caabaa5"],

